", "cd /hutian/ideawiki && git remote set-url origin \"${HT_FORGEJO_URL%/}$(git remote get-url origin | sed -E 's#^https?://[^/]+##')\"; timeout 90 git pull -q 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline|head -2; git diff 9a3fb93 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-3500"]], "output": "```console\na2b4cfc Brief rev. 17: HK check (like BA, two-factor reading unsupported); (b) form on new families\n17defa7 Brief rev. 16: P7 vs non-identification account worded as consistent-with; HK check weak support\n--- a/Brief.md\n+++ b/Brief.md\n-# Brief — idea of the study (revision 15: (b) degree-dispersion form, real-graph threshold not diagnosed; rev. 14: P7 verdict, inconclusive; rev. 13: reading of the frozen B₂ κ̂ at the grid floor, fixed before the block's results; rev. 12: P7 noise part as the analytic limit)\n+# Brief — idea of the study (revision 17: Holme–Kim check, two-factor reading not supported; (b) form holds on the new families; rev. 16: P7 wording 'consistent with'; rev. 15: (b) degree-dispersion form, real-graph threshold not diagnosed; rev. 14: P7 verdict, inconclusive; rev. 13: reading of the frozen B₂ κ̂ at the grid floor, fixed before the block's results; rev. 12: P7 noise part as the analytic limit)\n-  - **Follow-up results from existing cells (rev. 15, `analysis`, `experiment-repo`#7 items 2 and 3; exploratory-after-results, outside the P5 verdict; 60 runs each, Bernoulli designs, s = 0.5, σ = 0.5, first three graph draws).** *(b), bias against degree dispersion:* the tree-like form s·(HM(d)/AM(d) − 1), harmonic over arithmetic mean of the realised degrees, matches the regression's realised bias on (b) in all 60 runs (correlation 0.9988, RMS error 0.0073, mean |bias| 0.145). So the bias of (b) falls with d where the degrees are near-Poisson (SBM, ER: −0.115, −0.025, +0.005 at d = 5, 20, 80) because the dispersion shrinks relative to the mean, and does not fall where it does not (BA −0.16 to −0.12; Stanford3 −0.26 to −0.44, growing; ego-Facebook −0.27 to −0.38; near-regular WS ≈ 0). The paper states \"falls with d\" only with that condition. The formula is exact for tree-like neighbourhoods and was not tested against departures from that beyond these runs. *Real-graph threshold, (d):* the check does **not** show that the two real graphs straddle the threshold more than the synthetic ones (share within ±0.15 of θ 0.56–0.57 against 0.64–0.68 at d = 20); they have a wider exposure spread (SD of f 0.15–0.21 against 0.06–0.13) and a smaller regression bias (about 3× at d = 20, 1.3–2× at d = 80). Degree tail alone does not explain it (BA: spread 0.13, bias 0.68 ≈ ER) and clustering alone does not either (WS bias 0.78); the real graphs combine both and no cell varies both. **The cause is not diagnosed**, and the paper says so: the regression's failure on (d) does not transfer to the real graphs; the two-factor reading (tail and clustering together) is a hypothesis that no cell tests. At d = 5 the synthetic graphs also favour the learners, so the failure is specific to d = 20 and 80.\n-  - **P7 result (rev. 14, `analysis`, frozen coefficients from the 2142 original cells committed before the block ran; 666 block cells in 10 groups): INCONCLUSIVE under the rule as written.** (1) Absolute held-out R² of log|bias|: 0.115 (> 0, met; best benchmark p(1−p) 0.016, the other two degree benchmarks negative). (2) Gain over the best benchmark 0.099, group-level 95% CI [−0.059, 0.170]: not met. (3) Positive gain in 5 of 10 groups (HK, LN, a, c, d; 7 needed): not met. Per group the gain is largest where the degree benchmark is worst ((d) +0.52, (a) +0.28, the two new families +0.11 and +0.16) and negative on (e), (f), (g), (h), (b), where p(1−p) already explains much or everything is poor ((e) R² −0.5 for all predictors). The pre-registered S̄ (gain 0.088, CI [−0.077, 0.154], 5 of 10), the null-column S_adj (0.147, [−0.024, 0.218], 6 of 10) and corner × curvature alone (0.055) also fail criteria 2 and 3. **What the paper says:** S_adj is mildly informative about the bias in about half the groups and is not a confirmed predictor; \"S_adj predicts the bias out of sample\" is not claimed; the P5 verdict (no useful data-computable bias score) stands, now with a confirmatory test that does not overturn it. The non-identification acco\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "a0433243-0a46-5d0c-a45f-12c013315549", "at": 1795658044.3068266, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 132488, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "d74eab17cee594579d3c8167a89e26a7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "e945f1b4-e0b4-596c-8246-020af2e8fb16", "at": 1795658044.3125684, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 132489, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "d74eab17cee594579d3c8167a89e26a7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "f69029dc-3175-5c59-9078-805c901f0835", "at": 1795658044.3175607, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 132490, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "d74eab17cee594579d3c8167a89e26a7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "759cdfe8-f851-570b-809d-4126281e8804", "at": 1795658044.386193, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 132495, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "d74eab17cee594579d3c8167a89e26a